     <h1 class="title" title="Matheran Hill Station">Matheran</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/matheran-hill-station.jpg" title="Matheran hill station" alt="Matheran hill station, hill stations in india, 

west india hill stations, Matheran" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Alibag District, Neral At Mumbai, Maharashtra<br />
<b>Area:</b> 215 sq.kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Splendid Hill Station<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2500 ft above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 33&#176;C to 35&#176;C, Winter 12&#176;C to 15&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> March to May</p>     
<p><b>Matheran</b> was discovered by <b>Hugh Malet</b> in 1850. The British developed Matheran as a <b>popular tourist resort</b>. At an elevation of around 800m (2,625 ft) above sea level Matheran is a hill station located about 100 km from Mumbai. Matheran literally means jungle on top. All vehicles (Except emergency vehicles) are banned here. </p>

